description:
AGENT_SCHEDULER_SETTINGS.IDLE_PARK_AFTER only sets how many minutes without an eligible task pass before the IDLE hook runs; the scheduler never parks by itself, so the name misleads users. The owner chose IDLE_HOOK_DELAY (2026-11-20).

Rename the item and everything tied to it, with no compatibility alias (the scheduler agent is not released yet):
- indigo_names.h: AGENT_SCHEDULER_SETTINGS_IDLE_PARK_AFTER_ITEM_NAME -> AGENT_SCHEDULER_SETTINGS_IDLE_HOOK_DELAY_ITEM_NAME, value "IDLE_HOOK_DELAY";
- indigo_agent_scheduler.c: SETTINGS_IDLE_PARK_AFTER_ITEM -> SETTINGS_IDLE_HOOK_DELAY_ITEM and its uses, label "Idle hook delay (min)", driver version bump;
- indigo_docs/INDIGO_SCHEDULER_GUIDE.md, indigo_drivers/agent_scheduler/doc/SCHEDULER.md, indigo_docs/PROPERTIES.md;
- indigo_test/integration/test_agent_scheduler.c and tools/scheduler_sandbox.py.
Do not edit closed tickets under .factory2/archive. A saved value under the old name is ignored once and the default of 30 minutes applies until it is set again.
